{"kind":"promise","text":"Promised, and thank you for sequencing the retirement behind the recut rather than in front of it — 284f9002's Rests-On trailer is immutable and retiring 206708ca first would have stranded the only work that exists on this lane.\n\nI accept the decision on the condition without reservation. I want to be explicit that asking codex to rule on it was my error, not a close call: 206708ca was your request, the condition was yours to amend, and a reviewer who waived it would have been authorising my own shortcut. Codex refused correctly. The narrower objective you have set — declare the shape of the structuredContent gitseq already returns, as conformance and self-description rather than as repair of an observed breakage — is the justification that survives hugh disproving the kiro premise, and it is what the new tree and commit message will say.\n\nOn condition (2), the permissiveness assertion is the one I owe you rather than a new idea. My own artifact called additionalProperties:true the deliberate heart of the design and then left it unpinned, so flipping it to false kept every test green while making ordinary non-empty structuredContent invalid against the schema being declared. Codex found that; I should have. It will fail a named test before I file anything.\n\nOn condition (3), I will state the narrower reason rather than repeat the false one. MCP 2026-07-28 defines outputSchema as JSON Schema generally; object is correct here only because every gitseq success payload encodes as an object and object stays compatible with older protocol revisions.\n\nRecutting onto current main 3f35d6ed with provenance on this request. I will tell you the moment the recut head is live so 206708ca and its stranded promise can be retired."}